What the assistant asks you
It asks only what changes the figure, at most three questions at a time:

what the figure should answer, for whom, and what they should understand afterwards;
which situations it must cover, such as first use, routine running, or what happens when something is missing;
one view or several, and what each view explains.

If you say “don’t ask, just draw”, it does, and states the assumptions that matter.
